  "implementation": "Shared arc-length cubic fitting with position constraints, simple interior knots, existing five-diagonal portable/native solvers and exact rational stored-curve point admission. Gordon construction reuses original native intersection metadata, native rational approximation, knot insertion and explicit-tolerance compatibility. Piecewise affine knot mapping replaces the general composition helper that nudges nearby knots. Alignment precedes the single family basis union; full output knots and conservative tensor allocation bounds are retained.",
