  "limits": [
    "At most 64 distinct curve-fit constraint stations and 4096 controls. Targets must remain within the sampled-fit budget from their evaluated original source point; endpoint and retained-kink positions/handles stay fixed.",
    "Accepted constraint positions have exact rational stored-curve distance bounds at absolute numerical tolerance. General source-to-fitted-curve error remains adaptive sampled fitting, not a continuous source-image certificate.",
    "The Gordon surface admits complete images of its supplied input curves at the requested edge/interior tolerances. When those inputs are refitted curves, this certifies those fitted images, not an additional continuous bound against the pre-fit original curves.",
    "Raw Gordon parameter alignment remains piecewise affine and can retain kinks. Smooth common parameter fitting and Rhino interior comparisons remain unfinished; NetworkSrf is not registered in the application.",
    "Existing native source degree/control, weight/basis, prepared-curve, tensor allocation and exact-certificate work limits still apply. Collapsed mapped knot spans and inconclusive bounds reject.",
    "No new Rhino reference capture or Rhino fitting qualification is claimed. The oracle regression checks existing analytic fixture points and native construction.",
    "AddressSanitizer instruments SMLib, SM_API and adapter archives. Rust and separately bundled dependencies are not separately instrumented. Leak and optional stack-use-after-return checks are disabled."
  ],
